<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net11.0;net10.0;net9.0;net8.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<PackageId>Banned.Qbittorrent</PackageId>
		<Version>2.0.0</Version>
		<IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/banned2054/Banned.Qbittorrent</RepositoryUrl>
		<Authors>banned</Authors>
		<Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 banned</Copyright>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<Description>A .NET client library for qBittorrent's Web API</Description>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>
			Version 2.0.0 replaces the string-based application version with the ApplicationVersion type, a breaking change for version queries and direct TorrentService construction, and fixes setting file priorities.

			- Adds ApplicationVersion with numeric comparison, shared compatibility constants, and lossless round-tripping of server version strings.
			- Breaking: ApplicationService.GetVersion returns Task&lt;ApplicationVersion&gt; and raises FormatException for unparsable server versions.
			- Breaking: the TorrentService constructor now requires an ApplicationVersion, and QBittorrentClient.QbittorrentVersion has been removed.
			- Fixes torrents/filePrio sending the rejected ids parameter instead of id, which caused HTTP 400 responses.
			- Sends one filePrio request per file on servers below Web API v2.2.0, which reject batched file lists; earlier requests may already be applied on failure or cancellation.
			- Validates .NET 8, 9, 10, and 11 with 276 tests per target and the NativeAOT smoke application.
		</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageTags>qbittorrent;api;dotnet;httpclient</PackageTags>
	</PropertyGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
		<None Include="..\NOTICE" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
